cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the manuscript and the repository."
title: "NATRIX: Endpoint Priors, Split Protocols, and Deployment Audits in Inline HTTP Attack Detection"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a benchmark-validity study of inline HTTP attack
  detection. The package contains the endpoint-disjoint evaluation protocol and
  the paired interaction analysis, the feature-admission gates, the CPPP
  promotion protocol and TLA+ model, lexical and character-CNN baselines, CRS
  replay results, the v3-D positive control, the deployment audit ledger, and
  the manuscript build pipeline. All reported results are from public labelled
  HTTP corpora; no production or shadow-mode traffic is included.
